course: dictionary
lesson: 14004
title: Light without heat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Luminescence is a noun for light that something gives off without being hot. A glow-in-the-dark sticker glows, but it is not burning, and the glow does not come from a flame. «The stickers had a soft green luminescence in the dark bedroom.» The clues are glow and dark, so luminescence must be a cold kind of light.
explain: Some living things make their own luminescence. This is called bioluminescence, where bio means life. «Fireflies flashed their luminescence across the summer field.» A firefly is alive, and its light comes from inside its body, not from a fire.
explain: Test the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «The fireflies flashed their light without heat across the field». It still makes sense, so you have understood luminescence. A hot light bulb makes light by being very hot, so its light is not luminescence.
fact: Luminescence means light given off by something that is not hot.
fact: Bioluminescence is light made by living things, such as fireflies and some deep-sea fish.
fact: A hot light bulb or a fire gives off light too, but it is not luminescence, because it is hot.
fact: «Luminescence» is a noun, so it names a thing: the light itself.
fact: You can spot the clues: glow, glowing, and light in the dark often point to luminescence.
exercise: «The fireflies gave off a soft luminescence in the dark garden.» What is the luminescence here? | *Light given off without heat | A cool breeze at night | Loud buzzing sounds | Heat from a hot fire
exercise: Which of these is an example of bioluminescence? | A hot light bulb | *A firefly's glow | Sunlight on a hill | A lit birthday candle
exercise: Which kind of word is luminescence? | *Noun | Adjective | Adverb | Verb
test: A deep-sea fish makes its own light in the dark ocean. What do we call this light? | *Bioluminescence | Reflection | Shadow | Heat
test: A hot light bulb gives off light. Is this luminescence? | Yes, all light is luminescence | Yes, because it is bright | Only in the dark | *No, luminescence is light given off without heat
exam: «The glow-in-the-dark sticker shone with a green luminescence.» What does luminescence mean? | A loud crackling noise | *Light given off without being hot | Heat that you can feel on your hand | Dark shadows on the wall
